From 8f4addcd42abe160c6427598d55d9c1c51d1fb62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:32:17 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 46/62] Runtime: an overlay swapped out keeps its registrations

Swapping one 1.5 MB overlay for another dropped 390,000 registrations
(a walk over the whole table, an erase and a freed name each) and
registered as many again: a quarter of a second on the emulation thread
at every load between the menus and a battle, with the sound running dry.

Runtime::park_functions(key, start, end) takes an overlay's registrations
out as node handles, and restore_functions(key) puts them back when the
same overlay is loaded again: no allocation, one hash operation each.
unregister_functions clears a range address by address while every
registration is word aligned, and reserve_functions sizes the table before
a corpus registers. The overlay log line gives each swap's time.

<prefix>_NO_OVERLAY_PARKING drops and registers them, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
